## Topics and their protocol

Which protocol a topic is swept under is **declared here, not decided per module.** The
boundary test (*if a user can see it on a screen it is a surface; if it is only observable by
reading code or logs it is a mechanism*) still governs — but you apply it **once per topic**,
here, where the next author reads it instead of re-deriving it.

- `surface` — run `aidex-reference/references/01-discovery.md` (the visual pass is stage 4).
- `substitution` — run `02-architecture.md` **instead of** discovery rules 1, 2 and 4. The
  instrument becomes *running the code path*, and every claim must name **where** it was
  verified.

`environments:` is the list `substitution` topics may name. It is **checked**: a module under a
substitution topic that names none of them is reported, because "verified" is not a claim and
"verified in the backend container" is.

```topics
topic: features
protocol: surface

topic: architecture
protocol: substitution
environments: host, backend container, worker, dev, E2E

topic: backend
protocol: substitution
environments: host, backend container, worker, dev, E2E
```

> Declaring a topic `substitution` with no `environments:` is reported too — an environment
> axis nobody can check is an axis nobody will follow.

## Declaring ownership

Each reference module declares the items it **owns** in flat front-matter — **comma-separated**
`axis: item` entries, so the shared `validate.py` parser reads it without nested YAML:

```yaml
covers: "routes:/voices, routes:/voices/new, apps:lab_voices"
```

Split on the **first colon**, so both halves may contain spaces (`scheduled jobs: nightly`) and
an item may contain colons (`routes:/productions/:id`). Commas rather than whitespace because the
first version split on whitespace and **silently dropped** every multi-word axis this template
recommends — a fully documented project reported 100% gap with no warning. Unparseable entries
and entries naming an undeclared axis are now reported.

Ownership is **declared on sweep, never backfilled by inference.** Generating `covers:` by
grepping which document mentions which app reintroduces the exact mention-vs-describe
ambiguity the field exists to remove, and launders a guess into front-matter.

