## Verification

```bash
# 1. read the axis commands without running them
~/.claude/skills/aidex-reference/scripts/docs-census.sh --dry-run
# 2. approve this exact block (required once, and again after any edit to it)
~/.claude/skills/aidex-reference/scripts/docs-census.sh --trust --advisory
```

**Real output, {{DATE}}:** <!-- paste what you actually got. -->

How to read a change:

- **`REFUSED ... not been approved`** — expected before step 2, and expected again after any
  edit to the census block. Not a failure; the trust gate.
- **A `BROKEN` axis** — the command is wrong. A 100% figure from a broken axis is the exact
  failure this file exists to prevent, so fix the command before believing any number.
- **Every item in `gap` with `0 of N` modules declaring** — an adoption gap, not a coverage
  gap. Declare `covers:` on sweep; never backfill it by inference.

> Step 2 is why the second command carries `--trust`. An earlier version of this template ran
> `--advisory` alone and exited 3 on every fresh profile — a Verification block that cannot run
> as written, shipped in the file that teaches the contract. Caught 2026-07-30.
